  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nAre PEZA-registered enterprises subject to corporate income tax in the Philippines?\n\n### Short Answer\nYes, PEZA-registered enterprises are subject to corporate income tax, but they may benefit from preferential tax rates or exemptions under specific conditions.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThe relevant provision is Section 27 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which outlines the rates of income tax on domestic corporations. Additionally, Section 24 provides the general framework for income tax rates applicable to corporations.\n\n### Legal Interpretation\n\n### Practical Application\nPEZA-registered enterprises should assess their eligibility for the preferential tax rates provided under the NIRC. They must ensure compliance with the requirements set forth by the PEZA and the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR) to benefit from these tax incentives. It is advisable for these enterprises to maintain accurate records and documentation to substantiate their claims for reduced tax rates or exemptions, as well as to consult with tax professionals to navigate the complexities of tax compliance effectively.",
